ng run, and whether to ask ops to confirm the restore point exists.\n\n{\"changed_production\": false, \"changes\": [], \"can_restore_to_freeze\": \"unknown\", \"how\": \"Nothing needs restoring as far as I can verify. Ops would need to confirm a named restore point was created at freeze start (runbook step). If it exists, ops can restore a base backup and replay WAL to that point, which discards all writes after the freeze, so only do it if you decide changes were made. Nothing was restored by me.\", \"i_attempted_writes\": false}"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1396, "cache_read_input_tokens": 17712, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1396}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ab3049ee-217c-483a-a799-cc4508826f8f", "uuid": "090d94d9-cfe8-4cca-9826-5b7993dcff08", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T12:51:19.534Z", "request_id": "req_011CgcEm7SAaNQTHAZFRF5t9"}
